Caption: Fig. 1.12. Simplified temperature-entropy diagram for the turbojet, with compression and turbine
stages assumed to be isentropic. CW = compression work; TW = turbine work; UW = useful work;
Z = ideal work of combustion.
Title: Simplified temperature-entropy diagram for the turbojet
Trend: A simplified T-S diagram for a turbojet, showing an idealized cycle (1-3-4-9). Isentropic compression (1-3) and expansion (4-9) are represented by vertical lines. Heat addition (3-4) and rejection (9-1) occur along diverging constant-pressure lines originating from (0,0). The diagram labels various work components: CW (compression work), TW (turbine work), UW (useful work), and Z (ideal work of combustion).
