Caption: Fig. 3.23. Electron probe microanalysis (EPMA) maps of the transverse section of the as-cast structure of the CMSX-4 superalloy, which confirms the partitioning of W and Re to the dendrite core, and Ti and Ta to the interdendritic regions. (Courtesy of Mudith Karunaratne.)
Description: This figure contains four grayscale electron probe microanalysis (EPMA) maps of a CMSX-4 superalloy, showing the elemental distribution of Rhenium (Re), Tantalum (Ta), Titanium (Ti), and Tungsten (W). The lighter areas indicate higher concentrations of the respective element. The maps reveal that Re and W are concentrated in the dendrite cores (the star-shaped central regions), while Ti and Ta are segregated to the interdendritic regions. A scale bar indicates 200 μm.
