Caption: Fig. 3.31. The γ/γ' microstructures displayed by four experimental single-crystal superalloys of varying chemistries [28]. Note the correlation between the y' morphology and the estimated values of the lattice misfit, δ. (Courtesy of Pierre Caron.)
Description: This figure shows four micrographs of γ/γ' microstructures, illustrating the effect of lattice misfit (δ) on precipitate morphology. For alloys MC520 (δ=0.793%), MC544 (δ=-0.24%), and MC645 (δ=-0.315%), the γ' precipitates are cuboidal. For alloy MC534, with a larger negative misfit of δ=-0.665%, the precipitates are more rounded or spherical. Each micrograph has a 2 μm scale bar.
