Caption: Fig. 3.69. Persistent slip bands in a (001)-oriented single-crystal superalloy cycled at 700 °C [69], in which the y' particles are sheared.
Description: A transmission electron micrograph (TEM) showing persistent slip bands (PSBs) in a single-crystal superalloy. The PSBs appear as distinct, parallel bands cutting across the ordered γ' precipitate phase. The image includes annotations for crystallographic direction 'g = (111)', direction of 'Stress', and a '2 µm' scale bar.
