Caption: Fig. 4.15. Processing sequences for the production of F-101 compressor discs [13].
Description: A flowchart comparing three different processing sequences for producing F-101 compressor discs, showing the reduction in material weight at each stage. The sequences are: (1) Conventional processing (vacuum melting and cold forging), starting with a 95 kg ingot. (2) Hot isostatic pressing plus hot forging, starting with a 33 kg P/M preform. (3) Direct hot isostatic pressing, starting with an 18 kg near-net shape part. All routes result in a 5 kg finished part.
