Caption: Fig. 4.23. Schematic illustration of the distribution of the y' phase in a turbine disc alloy [19].
Description: A schematic diagram illustrating the microstructure of a turbine disc alloy, showing multiple gamma grains. Within each grain, there is a multi-modal distribution of gamma-prime (γ') precipitate phase: large primary γ' (1-10 µm) which are not solutioned; secondary γ' (70-120 nm) formed on cooling; and fine tertiary γ' (5-50 nm) precipitated at low temperatures. The gamma grains themselves are limited in size (5-22 µm) by Zener pinning from the primary γ' particles.
