Caption: Fig. 4.33. Fracture surfaces for the IN100 P/M superalloy tested in low-cycle fatigue at 0.5 Hz with R = 0.05 [27]. (a), (b) SEM images of the {001} fracture surfaces typical of failure at 538°C, showing the presence of cuboidal facets belonging to the y' phase. (c) {111} fracture surface typical of fatigue crack growth at room temperature – note that the fracture path is parallel to the traces of the slip lines in the top right of the image.
Description: Three SEM micrographs of fracture surfaces in IN100 P/M superalloy. Images (a) and (b) show {001} fracture surfaces from a 538°C test, characterized by cuboidal facets of the γ' phase (scale bars 10µm and 6µm respectively). Image (c) shows a {111} fracture surface from a room temperature test, with a crack path that is parallel to slip line traces (scale bar 20µm).
